            "rationale": "The waiver rules (which fine can be waived, a required approver, a waived fine taking no further payments, waived amounts not counting as owed) are placed in Tier 2 (Waivers.waive, Accounts.payable/owed/allocation/isSettled) and Tier 1 (the Waiver type). Tier 3 Views.account, however, extends its own status derivation: it checks waiverFor and then `covered = fine.Amount`, which restates Tier 2's isSettled predicate instead of asking Tier 2 for the fine's status. The two agree. The CLI borrow branch now asks Tier 2 (Accounts.isBlocked) instead of recomputing the balance itself, which removes an earlier re-decision in Tier 4.",
